# Official Knowledge Guide: Ftsc Scheme And Performance Overview

## Topic
Fast Track Special Courts (FTSC) Scheme

## Portals
[
  {
    "name": "Department of Justice FTSC Dashboard",
    "url": "https://dashboard.doj.gov.in/fast-track-special-court/"
  },
  {
    "name": "DoJ Scheme Portal",
    "url": "https://doj.gov.in/fast-track-special-court-ftsc/"
  }
]

## Scheme Background
{
  "launch_date": "October 2019",
  "nature": "Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS) funded under the Nirbhaya Fund framework",
  "nodal_department": "Department of Justice, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India",
  "primary_mandate": "Expeditious trial and disposal of pending rape cases under Indian Penal Code (IPC) / Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) and offences under the Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act, 2012",
  "cabinet_extension": "Approved by Union Cabinet on 29th November 2023 for continuation up to 31st March 2026",
  "financial_outlay": "Total outlay of ₹1,952.23 Crore (Central share of ₹1,207.24 Crore funded from the Nirbhaya Fund)",
  "prior_extension_2023_2026": {
    "approval_date": "2023-11-29",
    "approved_by": "Union Cabinet chaired by Prime Minister",
    "duration": "1st April 2023 to 31st March 2026",
    "financial_outlay": "₹1,952.23 Crore (Central share of ₹1,207.24 Crore from Nirbhaya Fund)"
  },
  "current_extension_2026_2031": {
    "status": "VERIFIED_CABINET_APPROVAL",
    "approved_by": "Union Cabinet chaired by Prime Minister",
    "duration": "1st April 2026 to 31st March 2031 (5-year continuation)",
    "total_financial_outlay": "₹3,788.04 Crore",
    "funding_breakdown": {
      "central_share_nirbhaya_fund": "₹2,353.15 Crore",
      "state_ut_share": "₹1,434.89 Crore"
    },
    "expansion_target": "Scaling from ~779-782 functional courts to 850 Fast Track Special Courts across participating States/UTs",
    "court_staffing_norm": "Dedicated Judicial Officer, exclusive Special Public Prosecutor, and 6 support staff per court"
  }
}

## Operational Framework
{
  "funding_pattern": "Centrally Sponsored Scheme sharing pattern: 60:40 between Centre and States (90:10 for North Eastern and Himalayan States/UTs; 100% Central funding for Union Territories without legislature)",
  "statutory_mandate": "Section 35 of the POCSO Act, 2012 mandates that recording of evidence of the child should be completed within 30 days and the trial should be completed within one year from the date of taking cognizance",
  "court_types": [
    "Exclusive POCSO Courts: Setup exclusively in districts where pending POCSO cases exceed 100",
    "FTSCs handling both Rape and POCSO matters: Setup in districts where caseload involves combined sexual assault offenses"
  ],
  "special_provisions": [
    "Child-friendly courtroom environment and vulnerable witness deposition complexes",
    "Separate waiting rooms for victim and accused to prevent visual contact and intimidation",
    "Support persons and special public prosecutors dedicated to child victims"
  ]
}

## National Performance Snapshot
{
  "reference_date": "2026-11-08",
  "total_states_covered": 32,
  "total_functional_courts": 782,
  "functional_exclusive_pocso_courts": 413,
  "cumulative_disposal_since_inception": 413265,
  "total_cases_pending": 246462,
