# Official Knowledge Guide: Live Streaming Guidelines And Rules

## Topic
Live Streaming of Court Cases

## Legal Framework
{
  "constitutional_basis": "Article 21 (Right to Fair Trial/Access to Justice), Article 145(4) (Open Court Principle)",
  "landmark_judgment": "Swapnil Tripathi & Ors. v. Supreme Court of India (2018) 10 SCC 639",
  "key_bench": "Three-Judge Bench headed by CJI Dipak Misra",
  "subsequent_implementation": "Constitution Bench hearings commenced live streaming on 27th September 2022"
}

## Model Rules
{
  "title": "Model Rules for Live Streaming and Recording of Court Proceedings",
  "issuing_authority": "e-Committee, Supreme Court of India",
  "date_of_formulation": "2021 (revised September 2022)",
  "source_file": "model_rules_for_live_streaming_and_recording_court_proceedings.pdf",
  "exclusions": [
    "Matrimonial disputes, child adoption, and child custody",
    "Cases concerning sexual offences (Sec 376 IPC / BNS)",
    "Cases of gender-based violence against women",
    "POCSO Act and Juvenile Justice Act proceedings",
    "Medical Termination of Pregnancy Act matters",
    "In-camera proceedings (Sec 327 CrPC / Sec 153B CPC)",
    "Matters where publication is antithetical to justice",
    "Cases provoking communal enmity or public order disturbance",
    "Recording of witness evidence and cross-examinations",
    "Privileged communications between advocate and client"
  ],
  "technical_standards": {
    "camera_angles": "Minimum 5 angles in courtroom (Judge, Advocate podium, Witness box, Accused, Overview)",
    "time_delay_buffer": "Live feed transmitted with a 10-minute delay to permit redaction/interruption if needed",
    "archival_storage": "Official court repository / DCR (Dedicated Control Room)"
  },
  "copyright_and_restrictions": {
    "copyright_owner": "Exclusive copyright belongs to the High Court / Court concerned",
    "unauthorized_use": "Recording, downloading, sharing, editing, or monetizing without written permission constitutes contempt of court and criminal offense under the Information Technology Act, 2000"
  }
}

## Official Viewing Portals
[
  {
    "court": "Supreme Court of India",
    "portal": "Official NIC Webcast Portal",
    "url": "https://webcast.gov.in/scindia/"
  },
  {
    "court": "Supreme Court of India",
    "portal": "Official Supreme Court YouTube Channel",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/@SupremeCourtofIndia"
  },
  {
    "court": "High Court of Gujarat",
    "portal": "Official YouTube Channel",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/@GujaratHighCourtLive"
  },
  {
