# Official Knowledge Guide: Traffic Challans And Vcourts Guide

## Topic
Traffic Violation Challans and Virtual Courts System

## Portals
[
  {
    "name": "Virtual Courts Portal (eCourts)",
    "url": "https://vcourts.gov.in/virtualcourt/",
    "faq_url": "https://vcourts.gov.in/virtualcourt/faq.php"
  },
  {
    "name": "MoRTH Parivahan eChallan Portal",
    "url": "https://echallan.parivahan.gov.in/"
  }
]

## Virtual Court Concept
{
  "definition": "A Virtual Court is an online court platform designed to eliminate the physical presence of a litigant or lawyer in the courtroom for adjudicating petty offenses, specifically traffic challans and transport department notices.",
  "presiding_officer": "Virtual Judge designated by the High Court who acts electronically on the digital summons and fine remittance.",
  "coverage": "31 Virtual Courts operational across 20+ States/UTs handling Traffic, Transport, and Notice violations."
}

## Search Methods
[
  {
    "search_by": "Mobile Number",
    "instruction": "Enter the mobile number registered at the time of challan generation. An OTP is sent for authentication to view all challans associated with that number."
  },
  {
    "search_by": "CNR Number",
    "instruction": "Enter the 16-character unique Case Natural Record number provided in the court summons SMS."
  },
  {
    "search_by": "Challan / Vehicle Number",
    "instruction": "Enter the Vehicle Registration Number (e.g., DL01AB1234) and Engine/Chassis number (last 4 or 5 digits) or Challan Number."
  },
  {
    "search_by": "Party Name",
    "instruction": "Enter the violator or vehicle owner name as recorded in the transport database."
  }
]

## Citizen Action Options
{
  "option_1_plead_guilty_and_pay_fine": {
    "process": [
      "View challan details, date of offense, violation section (e.g., speeding, red-light jumping, helmet violation), evidence photos/videos (if captured by automated ANPR/CCTV)",
      "Select 'I agree to plead guilty and pay fine'",
      "Proposed fine amount is displayed as determined by the Virtual Judge",
